.env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated by the test suites.
_scratch/

# Where runs land by default. Each run directory is a complete record of what was
# done to a real server, and some carry a secrets.json of generated database
# passwords in the clear.
/output/

# The same records, wherever else they end up: <YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>-<host>. Kept
# alongside the rule above because --runs-dir and DBA_RUNS_DIR can point anywhere.
#
# The digits are spelled out rather than globbed as 20*- so that a directory named
# after some other subject cannot be swallowed by the rule, and so the rule cannot
# stop matching in a later century. Deliberately not anchored with a leading
# slash: runs go to output/ by default, but --runs-dir and DBA_RUNS_DIR can put
# them anywhere, and this is the wrong file to be precise in at the cost of a leak.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/
